    "title": "Writing ‹ Florian Kiem",
    "markdown": "# Writing\n\nNotes, essays, and live experiments by Florian Kiem.\n\n- [The art of not shipping everything](https://floriankiem.com/writing/the-art-of-not-shipping-everything) (Sun May 17 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)) — We live in a time where everyone can build everything, building features got cheap, leading to many startups to believe shipping everything, all at once is the right approach.\n- [Products that look better used](https://floriankiem.com/writing/products-that-look-better-used) (Sat Jul 11 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)) — Most products look best the day you unbox them. Some are designed the other way around, they collect dents, creases, and scratches, and get more interesting the longer they are in use.\n- [Runs](https://floriankiem.com/writing/runs) — A live log of my runs since May 2026 — duration, distance, and the shape of each route. No map, no coordinates.\n\n---\n\nCanonical: https://floriankiem.com/writing\nMore for agents: https://floriankiem.com/llms.txt\n"
